<SiteLayout title="Teaching" description="Teaching experience and qualifications of Jason Laurie">
<section class="page-title">
    <div class="container">

                <h1 class="text-center"><strong>Teaching</strong></h1>

    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-heading">
    <div class="container">

                <h2 class="text-left">Teaching Qualifications</h2>

    </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">

            <div >
                <p>I am a senior fellow of the Higher Education Academy (SFHEA) and hold a Masters in Education (MEd) postgraduate degree with a research dissertation on alleviating the mathematics learning transition in higher education.</p>
            </div>

    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-heading">
    <div class="container">

                <h2 class="text-left">Previous Undergraduate and Postgraduate Teaching</h2>

    </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">

            <div >
                <p>Below is a list of my teaching responsibilities while at Aston University. They include a list of undergraduate and postgraduate courses taught in the mathematics department, as well as a variety of extracurricular employability skills workshops put on for our undergraduate students.</p>
            </div>

    </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">

            <div class="bullet-list">
                <ul>
                    <li>2024 - 2025: AM20LI Linear Mathematics (15 Credits,  Undergraduate Mathematics, Teaching Period 1) </li>
                    <li>2024 - 2025: AM30AP Approximation Theory (15 Credits, Undergraduate Mathematics, Teaching Period 2) </li>
                    <li>2021 - 2025: AM10PS Probability and Statistics (15 Credits, Undergraduate Mathematics, Teaching Period 1)</li>
                    <li>2021 - 2024: AM10DI Probability Distributions (15 Credits, Undergraduate Mathematics, Teaching Period 2)</li>
                    <li>2021 - 2024: AM41RS Specialist Research Skills and Techniques (15 Credits, Postgraduate Data Science, Teaching Period 1)</li>
                    <li>2016 - 2021: AM10PB Probability, (10 Credits, Undergraduate Mathematics, Teaching Period 1)</li>
                    <li>2016 - 2020: AM20NM Numerical Methods, (10 Credits, Undergraduate Mathematics, Teaching Period 2)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-heading">
    <div class="container">

                <h2 class="text-left">Extracurricular Employability Skills Courses</h2>

    </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section">

    <div class="container">

            <div class="bullet-list">
                <ul>
                    <li>An Introduction to Python (3-hour interactive lecture) - information can be found via the GitHub page <a href="https://github.com/AstonMath/Intro_Python"><img src="/assets/images/url_icon.png" alt="External link" height="20"></a></li>

                    <li>Python for Data Analytics (3-hour interactive lecture) - information can be found via the GitHub page <a href="https://github.com/AstonMath/Python_Data"><img src="/assets/images/url_icon.png" alt="External link" height="20"></a></li>

